<title>UK: UK notes in circulation rise 6.4 pct in week.</title>
<headline>UK notes in circulation rise 6.4 pct in week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>British bank notes in circulation rose 6.4 percent in the week to June 18 over the equivalent week a year ago, figures from the Bank of England showed. Last week the rise was 7.0 percent.(figures in rounded billions of stg) -  </p>
<p>			   Latest week  Previous week  Year-ago week</p>
<p> Notes in circulation  21.60	  21.64	     20.31</p>
<p> Bankers deposits	 2.55	   2.41		1.80</p>
</text>
